course: dictionary
lesson: 8170
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word resign is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «She decided to resign from her job at the shop so she could go back to school.» Resign from a job means you leave it by choice.
explain: The word resign can also mean you accept something bad that you cannot change. «Tom knew the match was lost, so he resigned himself to losing.» He did not like it, but he stopped fighting it. Look for words like yourself or be resigned to, and you will find this meaning.
explain: In chess, to resign means to give up the game before you are checkmated, because you know you will lose. The clues here are the chess pieces and the game. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Resign means to leave a job or position by choice, often by telling your employer in writing.
fact: To resign yourself to something means to accept something bad that you cannot change.
fact: In chess, to resign means to give up the game before checkmate.
fact: «To spend more time with family» is often the official reason given when someone is forced to resign.
fact: Resign is a verb, so it changes: resign, resigns, resigned, resigning.
exercise: «She decided to resign from her job at the shop so she could go back to school.» What does resign mean here? | To get a new job | To be paid more money | *To leave a job by choice | To fall asleep at work
exercise: «Tom knew the match was lost, so he resigned himself to losing.» What does resigned himself mean? | Won the match easily | Left the room in a hurry | Shouted at the referee | *Accepted that he could not change it
exercise: «Maya knew she could not win, so she resigned before checkmate.» Which chess meaning of resign is this? | She won the game | She moved her queen | *She gave up the game | She started a new game
test: The letter said, «To spend more time with family» is the reason he must resign. What does forced to resign suggest? | He was given a bonus for his work | *He was made to leave, even though he did not want to | He was asked to sing at a party | He chose to go on holiday
test: «After the rain cancelled the trip, Sam was resigned to staying indoors.» What does resigned to mean here? | *Sam accepted that he had to stay inside | Sam ran outside anyway | Sam asked for a new trip | Sam was very excited to stay inside
exam: Which sentence uses resign to mean leave a job by choice? | Mr Patel gave up the game before checkmate | Mr Patel knew the rain would never stop | Mr Patel felt resigned to the cold weather | *Mr Patel wrote a letter to resign from his post
